ion 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nJane's mother is very strict and always undermines her accomplishments at home. One day, Jane showed her mother the test paper on which she had scored 95 points out of 100. Her mother only said that she should have gotten full marks on such a simple test. However, when other parents are present, she openly talks about Jane's grades and excitedly praises her daughter.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Jane's mother ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Admiration\nB) Disappointment\nC) Jealousy\nD) Disgust\nE) Anger\nF) Nervousness\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Jane's mother feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) She is proud of her daughter's achievements\nB) She outperforms other parents in parenting style\nC) She wants to show off her skills in front of other parents\nD) She is better than her daughter","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.008577485540430153,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e8cbd6006945d280a618","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794369739319,"createTime":"2026-11-11 12:02:19","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"102dac7a4a7d4ee5bc17eac1fac792eb"}